  "note": "Recto page that is GENUINELY two-column for its top three quarters: the running prose (blocks n=1,2,3,4,5) is squeezed into a narrow LEFT column x 0.097-0.551, and a biography panel fills a RIGHT column x 0.579-0.873. Below the panel (from y 0.786) the text returns to the full measure x 0.098-0.688, so blocks n=8..n=12 are marked `full`. The biography panel (block n=7) has its own distinct fill: a MID cyan #9cdcf8, lighter than the #00adef accent but darker than the #c6eafb header band - three separate blues on one page, all sampled from flat interiors. The Coulomb portrait inside it is block n=6; its bbox lies inside the panel, and it is listed after n=7 because the panel is the container that is read first. The panel's far-right solid cyan #00adef bar carries 'CHARLES AUGUSTIN DE COULOMB (1736-1806)' in white type set sideways, recorded as major_heading like the EXAMPLE label bars on p007/p010. The panel's prose is about 0.85x body. Three displayed equations (n=4, n=9 with its right-ranged '(1.2)', n=11) and a footer_rule - the short dark #221f1f footnote separator at y 0.9077-0.9091, x 0.098-0.294 - above the starred footnote n=12. Folio '11' in a pale cyan box in the outer margin; '2022-23' recorded as running_header."
